            Color combinations based on mathematical rules of the color wheel:

            Analogous: neighboring colors on the wheel (±30°)

            Monochromatic: variations of the same color

            Complementary: opposite colors (180°)

            Split complementary: base color + 2 adjacent to the opposite

            Triadic: 3 evenly spaced colors (120°)

            Tetradic: 4 evenly spaced colors (90°)

