44 Safety indicators based on Behavior-Based Safety (BBS)`,verticalCompleteActivities:`1 Normative and legal foundations of occupational safety
  1.1 Consolidation of applicable Regulatory Standards
    1.1.1 Practical interpretation of NR‑01 and its general guidelines
  1.2 Principles of labor and criminal legislation in OHS
    1.2.1 Employer’s civil and criminal responsibilities
2 Management of occupational risks in complex environments
  2.1 Preliminary risk analysis methodologies (APR)
    2.1.1 Practical application of APR in industrial sectors
  2.2 Implementation of the risk matrix and controls
    2.2.1 Integration with quality management systems
3 Safety culture and organizational behavior
  3.1 Diagnosis of safety climate in companies
    3.1.1 Tools for measuring cultural indicators
  3.2 Employee engagement techniques
    3.2.1 Awareness campaigns focused on results
4 Ergonomics applied to safety and productivity
  4.1 Preliminary and in-depth ergonomic assessments
    4.1.1 Case study: ergonomics in administrative workstations
  4.2 Redesign of work stations and processes
    4.2.1 Tools for digital ergonomic simulation
5 Strategic planning in occupational safety
  5.1 Setting goals and performance indicators
6 Investigation and analysis of work accidents
  6.1 Data and evidence collection techniques
    6.1.1 Use of interviews and technical photographs in the process
  6.2 Application of the Cause Tree method
    6.2.1 Preparation of reports and corrective action plans
7 Emergency management and contingency plans
  7.1 Structuring teams and response routines
    7.1.1 Realistic simulations with structured feedback
  7.2 Integration of emergency plan with civil defense
    7.2.1 Sectorized communication protocols and alarms
8 Personal and collective protective equipment
  8.1 Technical criteria for selecting and replacing PPE
    8.1.1 Evaluation of comfort and effectiveness in practice
  8.2 Inspection and maintenance of collective protection equipment in critical lines
    8.2.1 Documented procedures and standardized checklists
9 Document management and process digitization
  9.1 Organization and control of reports and certifications
    9.1.1 Use of software for audit and traceability
  9.2 Data retention, access and security policy
    9.2.1 GDPR applied to OHS records
10 Communication and leadership in occupational safety
  10.1 Trainings and capacity building focused on safe leadership`,horizontalCompleteActivities:`1 Normative and legal foundations of occupational safety
